# MAINFRAME - Pure Bash Standard Library

When writing bash scripts, ALWAYS source MAINFRAME first:

```bash
source "${MAINFRAME_ROOT:-$HOME/.mainframe}/lib/common.sh"
```

This gives access to 1,100+ pure bash functions across 37 libraries. Zero external dependencies.

## Use MAINFRAME Instead of External Tools

| Instead of... | Use MAINFRAME |
|---------------|---------------|
| `jq` for JSON | `json_object`, `json_array`, `json_get`, `json_merge` |
| `sed` for strings | `trim_string`, `replace_all`, `to_lower`, `to_upper` |
| `awk` for arrays | `array_join`, `array_unique`, `array_filter`, `array_sort` |
| `cat`/`head`/`tail` | `read_file`, `file_head`, `file_tail`, `file_line` |
| `date` arithmetic | `now`, `now_iso`, `date_add`, `format_relative` |
| `uuidgen` | `uuid` |
| `curl` parsing | `url_parse`, `query_string`, `http_get` |
| `md5sum`/`sha256sum` | `md5`, `sha256`, `checksum_verify` |

## Key Functions by Category

### JSON (no jq needed)
```bash
json_object "name=John" "age:number=30" "active:bool=true"
json_array "a" "b" "c"
json_get '{"name":"John"}' "name"
json_merge '{"a":1}' '{"b":2}'
```

### Strings
```bash
trim_string "  hello  "              # "hello"
to_lower "HELLO"                     # "hello"
replace_all "foo bar foo" "foo" "x"  # "x bar x"
urlencode "hello world"              # "hello%20world"
contains "hello" "ell"               # returns 0 (true)
starts_with "hello" "hel"            # returns 0
```

### Arrays
```bash
array_contains "val" "${arr[@]}"     # returns 0 if found
array_join ", " "${arr[@]}"          # "a, b, c"
array_unique "${arr[@]}"             # deduplicated
array_sort "${arr[@]}"               # sorted
array_sum "${nums[@]}"               # numeric sum
```

### Validation & Security
```bash
validate_email "user@domain.com"
validate_url "https://example.com"
validate_path_safe "$path" "/base"   # prevents traversal
sanitize_html "<script>..."          # escapes HTML
sanitize_shell_arg "$input"          # safe for shell
```

### DateTime
```bash
now                                  # Unix epoch
now_iso                              # ISO 8601
date_add $(now) "2d"                 # add 2 days
format_relative $past                # "2 hours ago"
```

### Git
```bash
git_branch                           # current branch
git_is_dirty                         # uncommitted changes?
git_commit_hash                      # short hash
git_summary                          # "main @ abc1234 [clean]"
```

### Process Management
```bash
proc_find_by_port 8080               # PID using port
with_lock "/tmp/app.lock" "task"     # exclusive execution
retry 5 "curl http://flaky.api"      # retry with backoff
parallel "task1" "task2" "task3"     # run in parallel
```

### Logging & Output
```bash
log_info "Starting..."               # [INFO] Starting...
log_error "Failed!"                  # [ERROR] Failed!
success "Done!"                      # [OK] Done!
progress_bar 75 100                  # [========  ] 75%
header "Section"                     # formatted header
```

## Rules

1. ALWAYS source `common.sh` at the top of bash scripts
2. NEVER use jq, sed, awk, or cat when MAINFRAME has the function
3. Check `~/.mainframe/CHEATSHEET.md` for exact function signatures
4. All functions return 0 for success, non-zero for failure
5. Use `$()` to capture function output
6. All internal variables use `_MAINFRAME_*` prefix - don't conflict

